## Authorship and accountability

Per ICMJE, AI tools cannot be listed as authors. The human author bears full
responsibility for:

- Verification of every factual claim against primary sources (peer-reviewed
  literature, official documentation, professional standards) per the
  project's evidence hierarchy in `AGENTS.md`.
- Correctness of every statistical method and parameter choice.
- Identity hygiene for any pseudonymous author (no real-name metadata in
  committed files).

## Reproducibility log

All AI-assisted artifacts (figures, tables, analyses) carry a `Repro-Log-Path:`
trailer in their commit message pointing to the corresponding
`logs/reproducibility/repro_log_*.json` record. Each ReproLog captures:

- git HEAD at artifact generation
- `pip_freeze_sha256` (64-hex of the full venv freeze)
- Dataset checksums from `data/_manifest.json`
- RNG seed (if applicable)
- Model commit hash (if a fitted model was emitted)

Replay: check out the recorded git HEAD, restore the venv from
`logs/reproducibility/env/<sha>.txt`, restore the dataset by SHA matching
the manifest entries, and re-run.

